## 1. CRITICAL FIX — Info.plist (this causes crash + rejection)

Open your `Info.plist` (or Target → Info tab in Xcode) and add:

```xml
<key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
<string>Pixvera Pro uses your camera to scan documents with automatic edge detection.</string>
```

Why: `VNDocumentCameraViewController` (used in `ScanOCRStudioView`) accesses the camera. Without this key, the app **crashes immediately** when the reviewer taps "Scan Document" — this alone causes rejection under Guideline 2.1 (App Completeness).

You do **not** need `NSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription` since you correctly use `PhotosPicker` (the modern picker), which needs no permission entry.

## 2. CRITICAL FIX — Replace placeholder links

In `PreferencesView`, replace:
```swift
Link("Privacy Policy", destination: URL(string: "https://example.com/pixvera-privacy")!)
Link("Terms of Service", destination: URL(string: "https://example.com/pixvera-terms")!)
Link("Contact Developer", destination: URL(string: "mailto:support@pixvera.app")!)
```
with your **real, live** URLs once you host the Privacy Policy file (see below) and have a real support email. A dead/placeholder link is one of the top App Store rejection reasons (Guideline 5.1.1).

**How to host the Privacy Policy for free (pick one):**
- GitHub Pages (create a repo → enable Pages → drop the `.md` as `index.html` or convert to HTML)
- Notion → "Share to web" (public page)
- Google Sites (free, instant public URL)

## 3. App Store Connect — App Privacy Section

When filling the "App Privacy" questionnaire in App Store Connect, since the app collects **zero data**, select:
- **"Data Not Collected"** for all categories.

Do NOT leave this section unanswered — an unanswered privacy questionnaire is an automatic rejection.

